From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0140-no-deferred-clear-under-host-condition.patch

Source: 0140-no-deferred-clear-under-host-condition.patch
vk_rasterizer: do not defer a clear made under a host condition

Community patch 0098 (updates-2026-11-05/community), unchanged. The cause is from
nxnative PR 1299, which names it as Ocarina's white 3D scene.

A deferred clear becomes a render pass load op, and VK_EXT_conditional_rendering does
not apply to load ops. With a host predicate execute_on stays true, so a clear the GPU
should have skipped ran anyway. agl clears a depth target under a condition, copies the
prepass depth into it, and clears it again under the same condition, which the console
skips; run unconditionally, the main opaque pass's EQUAL test fails and the sky shows
through. Under a host condition the clear now goes through ClearAttachments, which is
predicated.

EDEN_NX2_DEFER_CONDITIONAL_CLEARS=1 restores the old behaviour for A/B runs (read with
getenv, so env.txt works in a release).

Not known yet: how many of Ocarina's conditions take the host path here. hcr_mode is 1
(exact) by default: a condition with queries still pending is evaluated on the CPU and
leaves hcr_is_set false, and this patch changes nothing for those. Only the host path
is affected.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
index d60866fafc..b505d75bc5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
@@ -1382,6 +1382,10 @@ void QueryCacheRuntime::View3DRegs(Func&& func) {
     }
 }
 
+bool QueryCacheRuntime::IsHostConditionalRenderingSet() const {
+    return impl->hcr_is_set;
+}
+
 void QueryCacheRuntime::EndHostConditionalRendering() {
     PauseHostConditionalRendering();
     impl->hcr_is_set = false;
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.h
index bbb5234e11..824bf2fa95 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.h
@@ -48,6 +48,9 @@ public:
 
     void ResumeHostConditionalRendering();
 
+    /// Whether the GPU predicates what is recorded now (which a render pass load op escapes).
+    [[nodiscard]] bool IsHostConditionalRenderingSet() const;
+
     bool HostConditionalRenderingCompareValue(VideoCommon::LookupData object_1, bool qc_dirty);
 
     bool HostConditionalRenderingCompareValues(VideoCommon::LookupData object_1,
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
index 06c8bfde4e..eee79b26f5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -1053,7 +1053,13 @@ void RasterizerVulkan::Clear(u32 layer_count) {
         clear_rect.rect.offset.x == 0 && clear_rect.rect.offset.y == 0 &&
         clear_rect.rect.extent.width >= render_area.width &&
         clear_rect.rect.extent.height >= render_area.height;
-    const bool can_defer_clear = ENABLE_DEFERRED_CLEAR && (!regs.clear_control.use_scissor || clear_covers_render_area) &&
+    // A deferred clear becomes a render pass load op, and conditional rendering does not apply to
+    // load ops: under a host condition it would always run. EDEN_NX2_DEFER_CONDITIONAL_CLEARS=1
+    // defers it all the same, as before.
+    static const bool defer_conditional = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_DEFER_CONDITIONAL_CLEARS") != nullptr;
+    const bool can_defer_clear = ENABLE_DEFERRED_CLEAR &&
+                                 (defer_conditional || !query_cache_runtime.IsHostConditionalRenderingSet()) &&
+                                 (!regs.clear_control.use_scissor || clear_covers_render_area) &&
                                  regs.clear_surface.layer == 0 &&
                                  !scheduler.IsRenderPassActive() &&
                                  (!use_color || color_full_channels) && ds_deferrable;
